  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}(x)+4y(x)=0,\\,y(0)=y(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?",
  "worked_solution": "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}(x)+P(x){y}^{\u2032}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{\u2032}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{\u2032}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{\u2032}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{\u2032}(a)={y}^{\u2032}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=0$ and $x=b=1.$\n\n$$\ny(0)=0,\\,y(1)=0\n$$\n\nThese are Dirichlet boundary conditions.",
